{
 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Neo4j Graph Database Tutorial\n","\n","This notebook demonstrates connecting to Neo4j Aura, creating nodes, creating relationships, querying graph data, filtering results, and deleting nodes. Each code cell is preceded by an explanation of its syntax.\n","\n","**Security:** credentials are loaded from environment variables. Never commit Neo4j passwords to a notebook or repository."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Install the Neo4j driver\n","\n","`%pip install neo4j` installs the official Python driver. The `%pip` form is preferred in Jupyter because it installs into the current notebook kernel. Restart the kernel if Jupyter asks you to.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `%pip install package-name` installs a Python package from a notebook cell."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["%pip install neo4j"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Import `GraphDatabase`\n","\n","`from package import name` imports a specific object from a Python package. `GraphDatabase` is the factory used to create a Neo4j driver.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `from module import object`."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from neo4j import GraphDatabase"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Configure connection settings\n","\n","The three variables contain the Aura URI, username, and password. `os.getenv()` reads values from environment variables instead of hard-coding secrets.\n","\n","Set these before starting Jupyter, for example: `NEO4J_URI=...`, `NEO4J_USERNAME=...`, and `NEO4J_PASSWORD=...`.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `os.getenv('NAME')` returns the value of environment variable `NAME`, or `None` when it is not defined."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","NEO4J_URI = os.getenv(\"NEO4J_URI\")\n","NEO4J_USERNAME = os.getenv(\"NEO4J_USERNAME\")\n","NEO4J_PASSWORD = os.getenv(\"NEO4J_PASSWORD\")\n","\n","if not all([NEO4J_URI, NEO4J_USERNAME, NEO4J_PASSWORD]):\n","    raise ValueError(\"Set NEO4J_URI, NEO4J_USERNAME, and NEO4J_PASSWORD first.\")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Create a Neo4j driver\n","\n","`GraphDatabase.driver()` creates the communication object used by Python to send Cypher queries to Neo4j. `auth=(username, password)` passes credentials as a tuple.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `object.method(argument=value)` calls a method with a named argument."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["driver = GraphDatabase.driver(\n","    NEO4J_URI,\n","    auth=(NEO4J_USERNAME, NEO4J_PASSWORD)\n",")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Verify connectivity\n","\n","`verify_connectivity()` checks whether the driver can reach Neo4j and authenticate successfully. It raises an exception when the URI, credentials, network, or instance status is incorrect.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `object.method()` calls a method without arguments."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["driver.verify_connectivity()"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Create a reusable query helper\n","\n","The function avoids repeating driver boilerplate. `parameters or {}` uses an empty dictionary when no parameters are supplied. `execute_query()` returns records, a summary, and column keys. `record.data()` converts each Neo4j record into a Python dictionary.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `def function_name(parameters):` defines a function; the indented lines form its body.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** parameters use `$name`, and Python supplies their values through `parameters_={...}`."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def run_query(query, parameters=None):\n","    records, summary, keys = driver.execute_query(\n","        query,\n","        parameters_=parameters or {}\n","    )\n","    return [record.data() for record in records]"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Create one student node\n","\n","The Cypher query creates a node with the `student` label and three properties. `s` is an alias for the node, and `RETURN s` sends the created node back to Python.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:**\n","- `CREATE (alias:Label {property: $parameter})` creates a node.\n","- `( )` represents a node.\n","- `:student` is a node label.\n","- `{...}` is a property map.\n","- `$name`, `$age`, and `$city` are parameters.\n","- Triple quotes (`\"\"\"`) allow a multi-line Python string."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","CREATE (s:student {name: $name, age: $age, city: $city})\n","RETURN s\n","\"\"\"\n","result = run_query(\n","    query,\n","    parameters={\"name\": \"SUDH\", \"age\": 21, \"city\": \"New York\"}\n,")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Reuse the query with different parameters\n","\n","The same Cypher statement can create another student because values are passed separately from the query. This is safer and more reusable than concatenating values into the query string.\n","\n","**Syntax:** a Python dictionary uses `{key: value}`; keyword argument `parameters=` passes it to the helper."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["run_query(\n","    query,\n","    parameters={\"name\": \"shadiya\", \"age\": 24, \"city\": \"BLR\"}\n,")"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 9. Prepare student data for bulk insertion\n","\n","`students` is a Python list containing dictionaries. Each dictionary represents one student. The dictionary keys match the Cypher parameter names used later.\n","\n","**Syntax:** `[...]` creates a list; `{...}` creates a dictionary; strings use quotes; commas separate items."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["students = [\n","    {\"student_id\": \"S001\", \"name\": \"Rahul\", \"age\": 24, \"city\": \"Bengaluru\"},\n","    {\"student_id\": \"S002\", \"name\": \"Priya\", \"age\": 23, \"city\": \"Delhi\"},\n","    {\"student_id\": \"S003\", \"name\": \"Aman\",  \"age\": 27, \"city\": \"Mumbai\"},\n","    {\"student_id\": \"S004\", \"name\": \"Sneha\", \"age\": 25, \"city\": \"Bengaluru\"}\n,"]
  },
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 10. Create students in a loop\n","\n","`CREATE` runs once per dictionary. The `for` loop assigns each dictionary to `student`, then passes it directly as the parameter map.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `CREATE (s:student {...}) RETURN s`. Re-running this cell creates duplicates because `CREATE` always creates a new node. Use `MERGE` for idempotent loads."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","CREATE (s:student {student_id: $student_id, name: $name, age: $age, city: $city})\n","RETURN s\n","\"\"\"\n","for student in students:\n","    run_query(query, parameters=student)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 11. Prepare course data\n","\n","Each dictionary contains a course identifier and name. The list will be processed in the next cell.\n","\n","**Syntax:** list elements can be dictionaries, and dictionary values can be strings."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["courses = [\n","    {\"course_id\": \"C001\", \"name\": \"Agentic AI\"},\n","    {\"course_id\": \"C002\", \"name\": \"Data Science\"},\n","    {\"course_id\": \"C003\", \"name\": \"Backend Engineering\"}\n,"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 12. Create course nodes\n","\n","The loop executes the parameterized Cypher query for every course. `c` is the node alias and `course` is the node label.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `CREATE (c:course {course_id: $course_id, name: $name}) RETURN c`."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"CREATE (c:course {course_id: $course_id, name: $name}) RETURN c\"\"\"\n","for course in courses:\n","    run_query(query, parameters=course)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 13. Prepare skill names\n","\n","`skills` is a list of strings. Each string will become the `name` property of a `skill` node.\n","\n","**Syntax:** a string list is written as `['value1', 'value2']`."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["skills = [\n","    \"Python\",\n","    \"Machine Learning\",\n","    \"RAG\",\n","    \"Neo4j\",\n","    \"FastAPI\",\n","    \"LangGraph\"\n,"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 14. Create skill nodes\n","\n","The loop passes a one-item dictionary because the query expects the `$name` parameter.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `CREATE (s:skill {name: $name}) RETURN s`. Labels and property values are case-sensitive, so `Neo4j` and `neo4j` are different values."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"CREATE (s:skill {name: $name}) RETURN s\"\"\"\n","for skill in skills:\n","    run_query(query, parameters={\"name\": skill})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 15. Prepare mentor data\n","\n","The mentor is represented by one dictionary. `mentor_id` is a stable identifier that is preferable to using a name for future matching.\n","\n","**Syntax:** dictionary keys are accessed with `dictionary['key']` when needed."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["mentor = {\n","    \"mentor_id\": \"M001\",\n","    \"name\": \"Sudhanshu\",\n","    \"company\": \"Euron\"\n,"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 16. Create a mentor node\n","\n","This creates a node with the `mentor` label and three properties.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `CREATE (m:mentor {...}) RETURN m`; `m` is the alias returned by the query."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"CREATE (m:mentor {mentor_id: $mentor_id, name: $name, company: $company}) RETURN m\"\"\"\n","run_query(query, parameters=mentor)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 17. Create an enrollment relationship\n","\n","The first two `MATCH` clauses find existing nodes. `MERGE` creates the relationship only when it does not already exist.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:**\n","- `MATCH (s:student {...})` finds a student.\n","- `MATCH (c:course {...})` finds a course.\n","- `MERGE (s)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(c)` creates a directed relationship.\n","- `(s)` and `(c)` are nodes; `[:ENROLLED_IN]` is a typed relationship; `->` shows direction.\n","- If either `MATCH` finds nothing, the query produces no row and no relationship."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student {student_id: $student_id})\n","MATCH (c:course {course_id: $course_id})\n","MERGE (s)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(c)\n","RETURN s, c\n","\"\"\"\n","run_query(query, parameters={\"student_id\": \"S001\", \"course_id\": \"C001\"})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 18. Add properties to a relationship\n","\n","`r` is an alias for the relationship, allowing `SET` to add or update relationship properties. `date($enrolled_on)` converts an ISO date string into a Neo4j date value.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:**\n","- `MERGE (s)-[r:ENROLLED_IN]->(c)` binds the relationship to `r`.\n","- `SET r.property = value` updates a property.\n","- Multiple assignments can be separated by commas.\n","- `RETURN s, c` returns both endpoint nodes."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student {student_id: $student_id})\n","MATCH (c:course {course_id: $course_id})\n","MERGE (s)-[r:ENROLLED_IN]->(c)\n","SET r.enrolled_on = date($enrolled_on),\n","    r.status = $status,\n","    r.grade = $grade,\n","    r.remarks = $remarks\n","RETURN s, c\n","\"\"\"\n","run_query(query, parameters={\n","    \"student_id\": \"S001\", \"course_id\": \"C001\",\n","    \"enrolled_on\": \"2024-06-01\", \"status\": \"active\",\n","    \"grade\": \"A\", \"remarks\": \"Excellent performance\"\n,"})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 19. Prepare multiple enrollments\n","\n","Each dictionary maps a student ID to a course ID. `S005` is intentionally included as an example of a missing node; its relationship will not be created unless that student exists.\n","\n","**Syntax:** dictionary keys can use any names, but the next cell maps them to Cypher parameter names."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["enrollments = [\n","    {\"student\": \"S001\", \"course\": \"C001\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S002\", \"course\": \"C002\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S003\", \"course\": \"C003\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S004\", \"course\": \"C003\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S005\", \"course\": \"C002\"}\n,"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 20. Create enrollments in a loop\n","\n","For every enrollment, `MATCH` finds both endpoints and `MERGE` creates the edge. The nested dictionary access uses `enrollment['student']` and `enrollment['course']`.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `MERGE` is idempotent for the same pattern, so rerunning the cell does not create another identical relationship. Always verify IDs and capitalization."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student {student_id: $student_id})\n","MATCH (c:course {course_id: $course_id})\n","MERGE (s)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(c)\n","RETURN s, c\n","\"\"\"\n","for enrollment in enrollments:\n","    run_query(query, parameters={\n","        \"student_id\": enrollment[\"student\"],\n","        \"course_id\": enrollment[\"course\"]\n","    })"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 21. Create student-skill relationships\n","\n","This models a many-to-many relationship: one student can have many skills, and one skill can belong to many students. `HAS_SKILL` is directed from student to skill.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `MATCH` binds existing nodes to aliases; `MERGE (s)-[r:HAS_SKILL]->(sk)` creates or reuses the relationship; `RETURN` shows both nodes."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["student_skills = [\n","    {\"student\": \"S001\", \"skill\": \"Python\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S001\", \"skill\": \"RAG\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S001\", \"skill\": \"LangGraph\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S002\", \"skill\": \"Python\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S002\", \"skill\": \"Neo4j\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S003\", \"skill\": \"Python\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S003\", \"skill\": \"Machine Learning\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S004\", \"skill\": \"FastAPI\"},\n","    {\"student\": \"S004\", \"skill\": \"Python\"}\n,"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student {student_id: $student_id})\n","MATCH (sk:skill {name: $skill})\n","MERGE (s)-[:HAS_SKILL]->(sk)\n","RETURN s, sk\n","\"\"\"\n","for student_skill in student_skills:\n","    run_query(query, parameters={\n","        \"student_id\": student_skill[\"student\"],\n","        \"skill\": student_skill[\"skill\"]\n","    })"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 22. Traverse from a student to their skills\n","\n","This is a read query. It starts at Rahul, follows outgoing `HAS_SKILL` relationships, and returns the student and every connected skill.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:**\n","- `MATCH (s:student {name: $name})` finds Rahul.\n","- `-[:HAS_SKILL]->` follows a directed relationship.\n","- `(sk:skill)` binds the destination node to `sk`.\n","- Property values such as `Rahul` are case-sensitive.\n","- `RETURN s, sk` returns two columns per matching relationship."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student {name: $name})-[:HAS_SKILL]->(sk:skill)\n","RETURN s, sk\n","\"\"\"\n","run_query(query, parameters={\"name\": \"Rahul\"})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 23. Filter students by age\n","\n","`WHERE` filters rows matched by `MATCH`. `AND` requires both comparisons to be true. Returning properties instead of `s` returns only selected values.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `s.age` accesses a property; `$age` and `$min_age` are parameters; `<=` and `>=` are comparison operators."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student)\n","WHERE s.age <= $age AND s.age >= $min_age\n","RETURN s.name, s.age\n","\"\"\"\n","run_query(query, parameters={\"age\": 25, \"min_age\": 18})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 24. Delete a student and attached relationships\n","\n","`DETACH DELETE` removes the matched node and all relationships connected to it. A plain `DELETE` fails when the node still has relationships. The empty list returned by the helper is expected because the query has no `RETURN` clause.\n","\n","**Cypher syntax:** `MATCH` selects the node; `DETACH DELETE s` deletes the node and its edges. Prefer matching by a unique ID rather than a non-unique name."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["query = \"\"\"\n","MATCH (s:student {name: $name})\n","DETACH DELETE s\n","\"\"\"\n","run_query(query, parameters={\"name\": \"Rahul\"})"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Key syntax summary\n","\n","- **Node:** `(n:Label {key: value})`\n","- **Relationship:** `(a)-[r:TYPE]->(b)`\n","- **Create:** `CREATE` always creates a new pattern.\n","- **Upsert:** `MERGE` matches an existing pattern or creates it.\n","- **Read:** `MATCH ... WHERE ... RETURN ...`\n","- **Update:** `SET n.property = value`\n","- **Delete:** `DELETE` or `DETACH DELETE`\n","- **Parameters:** use `$parameter` in Cypher and `parameters_={...}` in Python.\n","\n","For production data loading, add uniqueness constraints and prefer `UNWIND` for large batches."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":[]}
